  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#48516\", \"PowerToys#49053\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. After docking or undocking, the Command Palette Dock settings page often lists only the internal monitor, and the dock disappears or comes back empty (PowerToys#48516). A similar loss of monitors and per-monitor settings was reported after an RDP session (PowerToys#49053). The past tickets show no fix. The only workaround is the one you found: turn Command Palette off and on, or restart PowerToys, after reconnecting to the dock. In PowerToys#49053, restarting PowerToys eventually fixed the wrong display numbering and resolution. Add your details to PowerToys#48516, including your version 0.100.2 and the laptop-with-disabled-internal-display setup.\"}",
